 "journal": [
  {
   "date": "2026-10-07",
   "author": "Claude",
   "text": "What happened: First session of the plan, RANK INT A, all 24 runs. Medians were well under your baseline: Smooth Thin 375 (baseline 429), Air Track 150% 360 (447), Sphere S 557 (663).\nConditions: Played within 10 minutes of waking, f.lux on, a dimmed screen, no sound, hitmarker on then off for the last 4 runs. Five changes at once, so this session says little about your skill.\nRest: A first look at rest across all 97 runs from Oct 6 and 7. The first attempt on each scenario scores about 3% below its usual, and the first run after a 15+ minute break about 6% below. That's warm-up, not tiredness. Inside a scenario, runs after 20 s to 2 min of rest scored about 2% higher than runs started within 20 s, but that's too little data to trust yet. Time of day shows no pattern. Treat the first run on each scenario as warm-up and don't judge yourself on it.\nNext time: Change one thing at a time. Keep no sound if that's the goal, but play fully awake with normal brightness so the next sessions are comparable."
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-10-07",
   "author": "Ryan",
   "text": "Did Session 1. It was terrible. I played it within 10 minutes of waking up. I played with f.lux app on (which removes blue light) and with a lower screen light on my laptop because my girlfriend was sleeping. I also played with hitmarker on, but turned it off in the final 4 runs of my playlist because it was annoying. I also played without sound. Normally, I play benchmark scenarios without sound, but I want to build up my skill at reading the bot. I used to play without sound when I first started, but I'm starting again. If you have any feedback, stats you want to see, UI/UX feedback, dm me in discord"
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-10-07",
   "author": "Claude",
   "text": "Playlist: ZEUS BUILDER (14 runs, 12:24–13:59)\nWhat happened: First full play of the playlist. The three drills played before were all under their April–May medians: Close Fast Precise 1550 (was 1870), Thin Fast 1410 (1580), Ground Plaza 331 (346). The four new drills set their starting scores.\nConditions: A Steam sign-out stopped the session for 51 minutes. The run straight after dropped from 1645 to 1455, and Smooth Thin S was 123 after a 10-minute gap, then 162. No note on sleep or settings for this session.\nNext time: Play it in one go and treat each drill's first run as warm-up. On the snap drills, try relaxing before you reach the target, and write down whether you did."
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-10-07",
   "author": "Claude",
   "text": "Playlist: RANK INT A, second time today (24 runs, 20:27–21:34)\nWhat happened: Much better than this morning. Medians: Smooth Thin 418 (morning 375), Air Track 481 (360), Sphere S 706 (557). Air Track and Sphere S beat their pre-plan baselines (447 and 663), and Smooth Thin was just under (429). Best runs: 464, 537 and 780.\nConditions: Evening, wide awake, about 15 hours after the morning's just-woke-up session. No note on screen, sound or hitmarker, so the exact differences aren't known.\nRest: Ryan lengthened his rests on purpose after reading the rest table. His median rest between runs of the same scenario went from 16 s this morning to 54 s. Across all 121 runs so far, rests of 20 s to 2 min score about 3% above rests under 20 s, so it's worth keeping. Tonight's jump was 11–34%, though, and within the session longer-rest runs weren't clearly better. Most of the gain came from playing awake with normal settings.\nNext time: Keep whatever you did tonight, and write it down so it can be repeated. The morning was conditions, not skill. The first run of each scenario was again the lowest, so keep treating it as warm-up."
  }
 ],
